From: AshesTom <258768419+AshesTom@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] rpcrt4: name the account for Negotiate and Kerberos in RpcServerInqDefaultPrincName

Purpose: XP's Security Center service (wscsvc.dll) registers its
authentication with Negotiate's principal name; it stopped when the call
failed.
Windows behavior: RpcServerInqDefaultPrincName gives the process account's
name for RPC_C_AUTHN_GSS_NEGOTIATE and RPC_C_AUTHN_GSS_KERBEROS as for NTLM.
Wine before: only RPC_C_AUTHN_WINNT, RPC_S_UNKNOWN_AUTHN_SERVICE otherwise.
Change: the same account name for the three.
Scope: RpcServerInqDefaultPrincNameA/W.
---
diff --git a/dlls/rpcrt4/rpc_server.c b/dlls/rpcrt4/rpc_server.c
--- a/dlls/rpcrt4/rpc_server.c
+++ b/dlls/rpcrt4/rpc_server.c
@@ -1506,7 +1506,11 @@
 
     FIXME("%lu, %p\n", AuthnSvc, PrincName);
 
-    if (AuthnSvc != RPC_C_AUTHN_WINNT) return RPC_S_UNKNOWN_AUTHN_SERVICE;
+    /* Negotiate and Kerberos name the account too (XP's Security Center,
+     * wscsvc.dll, asks Negotiate's). */
+    if (AuthnSvc != RPC_C_AUTHN_WINNT && AuthnSvc != RPC_C_AUTHN_GSS_NEGOTIATE &&
+        AuthnSvc != RPC_C_AUTHN_GSS_KERBEROS)
+        return RPC_S_UNKNOWN_AUTHN_SERVICE;
 
     GetUserNameExW( NameSamCompatible, NULL, &len );
     if (GetLastError() != ERROR_MORE_DATA) return RPC_S_INTERNAL_ERROR;
